{"id":"other-pay-spikes-by-department","title":"Spikes in other pay, by department","tier":"REDFLAG","question":"In which departments do one-year spikes in other pay occur, and how many are payouts on leaving?","finding":"29 departments have at least one spike. Police has 52 of the 70 mid-career ones and 145 in all ($11.7 million); next come Public Health (31, of which 17 on leaving), Public Defender (4, of which 1 on leaving) and District Attorney (13, of which 10 on leaving). Outside Police, 18 of 146 spike years were followed by more work; the rest are payouts on leaving or fall in the latest year.","how":"The spikes of the previous table counted by the department of the person’s main row in the spike year. “People followed” is the number of followable employees with four or more years whose last year was in the department; the rate is spikes for every 1,000 of them. Ranked by mid-career cases.","limits":"The same explanations apply as in the previous table. Departments whose agreements allow larger balances of leave to be carried show larger payouts on leaving; the agreements are not on disk. A small department can show a high rate on one or two people.","columns":[{"k":"department","t":"Department","type":"text"},{"k":"spikes","t":"Spike years","type":"int"},{"k":"working","t":"Still working afterwards","type":"int"},{"k":"leaving","t":"On leaving","type":"int"},{"k":"latest","t":"Latest year: too soon to tell","type":"int"},{"k":"money","t":"Other pay in those years","type":"usd"},{"k":"followed","t":"People followed","type":"int"},{"k":"per1000","t":"Spikes per 1,000 followed","type":"times"},{"k":"largest","t":"Largest","type":"usd"},{"k":"largestYear","t":"In fiscal year","type":"year"},{"k":"largestJob","t":"Job class","type":"text"}],"rows":[{"department":"Police","spikes":145,"leaving":43,"working":52,"latest":50,"money":11708591,"followed":1997,"per1000":72.6,"largest":203731,"largestYear":2026,"largestJob":"Dep Dir IV (class 0954)"},{"department":"Publ